{"path":"/documentation/intervention/errors","section":"documentation","title":"errors","description":"Documentation for the nnsight Python library","toc":[{"id":"nnsight.intervention.errors","label":"errors","depth":2},{"id":"nnsight.intervention.errors.DeferredError","label":"DeferredError","depth":3},{"id":"nnsight.intervention.errors.capture_exception","label":"capture_exception","depth":3},{"id":"nnsight.intervention.errors.raise_deferred","label":"raise_deferred","depth":3}],"segments":[{"type":"html","html":"<h2 id=\"nnsight.intervention.errors\" class=\"doc-heading\">\n<code class=\"doc-symbol doc-symbol-heading doc-symbol-module\"></code>            <span class=\"doc-object-name doc-module-name\">errors</span>\n\n\n</h2>"},{"type":"html","html":"<p>Carry a deferred worker exception back to the trace that wrote it.</p>\n<p>A deferring interleaver (<a title=\"            defer_exceptions\n\n\n  \n      instance-attribute\n  \" href=\"/documentation/intervention/interleaver#nnsight.intervention.interleaver.Interleaver.defer_exceptions\"><code>defer_exceptions</code></a>)\nrecords a worker's exception on its mediator instead of raising it out of the\nhook, so the driver can end just that worker's request. The error still has to\nreach the client that wrote the intervention — which may be another process — so\nit is reduced to a plain, picklable dict in the worker and re-raised at the client.</p>\n<p>What the client catches is a <code>RuntimeError</code> whose message <em>starts</em> with the\noriginal type name and message, so a caller that needs to tell one refusal from\nanother matches on the text rather than on the class.</p>\n<p>A <code>tracer.stop()</code> raises <a title=\"            EarlyStopException\" href=\"/documentation/intervention/interleaver#nnsight.intervention.interleaver.EarlyStopException\"><code>EarlyStopException</code></a>,\nwhich travels the same path but is control flow, not an error: it is marked and\nnever re-raised.</p>"},{"type":"html","html":"<h3 id=\"nnsight.intervention.errors.DeferredError\" class=\"doc-heading\">\n<code class=\"doc-symbol doc-symbol-heading doc-symbol-class\"></code>            <span class=\"doc-object-name doc-class-name\">DeferredError</span>\n\n\n</h3>"},{"type":"html","html":"<p class=\"doc-class-bases\">\n              Bases: <code><span title=\"typing.TypedDict\">TypedDict</span></code></p>"},{"type":"html","html":"<h4 id=\"nnsight.intervention.errors.DeferredError.type_name\" class=\"doc-heading\">\n<code class=\"doc-symbol doc-symbol-heading doc-symbol-attribute\"></code>            <span class=\"doc-object-name doc-attribute-name\">type_name</span>\n\n\n  <span class=\"doc-labels\">\n      <small class=\"doc-label doc-label-instance-attribute\"><code>instance-attribute</code></small>\n  </span>\n\n</h4>"},{"type":"code","lang":"python","code":"type_name: str"},{"type":"html","html":"<div class=\"doc-contents\">\n\n    </div>"},{"type":"html","html":"<h4 id=\"nnsight.intervention.errors.DeferredError.message\" class=\"doc-heading\">\n<code class=\"doc-symbol doc-symbol-heading doc-symbol-attribute\"></code>            <span class=\"doc-object-name doc-attribute-name\">message</span>\n\n\n  <span class=\"doc-labels\">\n      <small class=\"doc-label doc-label-instance-attribute\"><code>instance-attribute</code></small>\n  </span>\n\n</h4>"},{"type":"code","lang":"python","code":"message: str"},{"type":"html","html":"<div class=\"doc-contents\">\n\n    </div>"},{"type":"html","html":"<h4 id=\"nnsight.intervention.errors.DeferredError.traceback\" class=\"doc-heading\">\n<code class=\"doc-symbol doc-symbol-heading doc-symbol-attribute\"></code>            <span class=\"doc-object-name doc-attribute-name\">traceback</span>\n\n\n  <span class=\"doc-labels\">\n      <small class=\"doc-label doc-label-instance-attribute\"><code>instance-attribute</code></small>\n  </span>\n\n</h4>"},{"type":"code","lang":"python","code":"traceback: str"},{"type":"html","html":"<div class=\"doc-contents\">\n\n    </div>"},{"type":"html","html":"<h4 id=\"nnsight.intervention.errors.DeferredError.is_control_flow\" class=\"doc-heading\">\n<code class=\"doc-symbol doc-symbol-heading doc-symbol-attribute\"></code>            <span class=\"doc-object-name doc-attribute-name\">is_control_flow</span>\n\n\n  <span class=\"doc-labels\">\n      <small class=\"doc-label doc-label-instance-attribute\"><code>instance-attribute</code></small>\n  </span>\n\n</h4>"},{"type":"code","lang":"python","code":"is_control_flow: bool"},{"type":"html","html":"<div class=\"doc-contents\">\n\n    </div>"},{"type":"html","html":"<h3 id=\"nnsight.intervention.errors.capture_exception\" class=\"doc-heading\">\n<code class=\"doc-symbol doc-symbol-heading doc-symbol-function\"></code>            <span class=\"doc-object-name doc-function-name\">capture_exception</span>\n\n\n</h3>"},{"type":"code","lang":"python","code":"capture_exception(exception: BaseException) -> DeferredError"},{"type":"html","html":"<div class=\"doc-contents\">\n\n        <p>Reduce a worker's exception to a wire-safe dict.</p>\n<p>Uses the intervention-only traceback stashed by\n<a title=\"            switch\" href=\"/documentation/intervention/interleaver#nnsight.intervention.interleaver.Mediator.switch\"><code>switch</code></a> when present, so the\nsurfaced trace points at the user's line rather than the model/hook stack.</p>\n\n\n    </div>"},{"type":"html","html":"<h3 id=\"nnsight.intervention.errors.raise_deferred\" class=\"doc-heading\">\n<code class=\"doc-symbol doc-symbol-heading doc-symbol-function\"></code>            <span class=\"doc-object-name doc-function-name\">raise_deferred</span>\n\n\n</h3>"},{"type":"code","lang":"python","code":"raise_deferred(error: Optional[DeferredError]) -> None"},{"type":"html","html":"<div class=\"doc-contents\">\n\n        <p>Re-raise a captured worker error at the client; a stop returns silently.</p>\n<p>Raised as a <code>RuntimeError</code> carrying the original type, message, and\nintervention traceback rather than reconstructing the original class, which is\nbrittle across a process boundary.</p>\n\n\n    </div>"}]}